/-!
# The connected immersed subgroup of a Lie subalgebra

Let `G` be a finite-dimensional real Lie group with Lie algebra `𝔤`, and let `S ≤ 𝔤` be a Lie
subalgebra. Its left-invariant distribution `g ↦ d(L_g)₁ S` is the tangent distribution of a
foliation of `G` (`LieSubalgebra.mulInvariantFoliation`), whose leaf through the identity is a
subgroup, the integral leaf subgroup `LieSubalgebra.integralLeafSubgroup S`. This file proves that
this subgroup is a connected immersed Lie subgroup of `G` with Lie algebra `S`
(`LieSubalgebra.integralLeafSubgroupData`,
`LieSubalgebra.range_lieMapToHom_integralLeafSubgroupData`).
This is the existence half of the correspondence between Lie subalgebras and connected immersed
Lie subgroups; the uniqueness half is
`TauCeti.Lie.ImmersedLieSubgroupData.eq_of_range_lieMapToHom_eq`.

The left-invariant distribution of `S` is smooth, so the global Frobenius theorem gives the leaf
through the identity as a smooth integral manifold `L`, with its own intrinsic manifold topology,
injectively immersed in `G` (`TauCeti.IsInvolutiveDistribution.leaf`); its image is the integral
leaf subgroup (`TauCeti.Foliation.range_leaf_distribution`). The group structure of the subgroup
is transported to `L` along its parametrization. Multiplication and inversion of `L` are smooth
because, over a second-countable manifold, every smooth map with values in a leaf factors
smoothly through the leaf's intrinsic manifold structure
(`TauCeti.IsInvolutiveDistribution.existsUnique_contMDiff_factor_leaf`): the products and
inverses of points of `L`, computed in `G`, are smooth maps into `G`. So `L` is a Lie group and
its parametrization an injective immersive homomorphism. The image of its differential at the
identity is the fibre of the distribution there, which is `S`.

Second countability of `G` is part of the definition of a manifold in the reference below. The
presentation is modelled on Euclidean space, the model of the Frobenius leaf, while
`TauCeti.Lie.ImmersedLieSubgroupData` takes its source model in the universes of the model of `G`,
so the model of `G` is taken in `Type`.

## Main definitions

* `LieSubalgebra.integralLeafSubgroupData S`: the integral leaf subgroup of `S` as a connected
  immersed Lie subgroup, presented by the leaf through the identity with its intrinsic manifold
  structure.

## Main results

* `LieSubalgebra.range_lieMapToHom_integralLeafSubgroupData`: the differential of the
  presentation has range `S`.
* `LieSubalgebra.exists_immersedLieSubgroupData_range_lieMapToHom_eq`: every Lie subalgebra is the
  differential range of a connected immersed Lie subgroup.
* `LieSubalgebra.isImmersedLieSubgroup_integralLeafSubgroup`: the integral leaf subgroup is a
  connected immersed Lie subgroup.
* `TauCeti.Lie.ImmersedLieSubgroupData.eq_integralLeafSubgroup_of_range_lieMapToHom_eq`: every
  connected immersed Lie subgroup with differential range `S` is the integral leaf subgroup of `S`.
* `LieSubalgebra.integralLeafSubgroup_eq_closure_lieExp_image`: the integral leaf subgroup of `S`
  is generated by the exponentials of the elements of `S`.
* `LieSubalgebra.le_lieSubalgebraOfSubgroup_integralLeafSubgroup`: `S` lies in the Lie algebra of
  its integral leaf subgroup.
* `LieSubalgebra.range_lieMap_integralLeafSubgroupData`: the Lie map of the integral leaf subgroup
  of `S` has range `S`.
* `LieSubalgebra.commute_integralLeafSubgroupData_of_isLieAbelian`: the integral leaf subgroup of an
  abelian Lie subalgebra is commutative.
* `LieIdeal.commute_integralLeafSubgroupData_of_disjoint`: the integral leaf subgroups of two Lie
  ideals with trivial intersection commute with each other.

## References

* J. M. Lee, *Introduction to Smooth Manifolds*, 2nd ed., Springer (2013), Theorem 19.26,
  pp. 506–507: the connected Lie subgroup of a Lie subalgebra as the leaf through the identity of
  its left-invariant foliation.
* A. Kirillov Jr., *An Introduction to Lie Groups and Lie Algebras*, Cambridge Studies in
  Advanced Mathematics 113 (2008), Theorem 3.40.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open Set Function Manifold Module TauCeti TauCeti.Lie
open scoped ContDiff Manifold

universe w

namespace LieSubalgebra

attribute [local instance] LieGroup.minSmoothness_of_isRCLikeNormedField

section Leaf

variable {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E]
  {H : Type*} [TopologicalSpace H] {I : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H}
  {G : Type w} [TopologicalSpace G] [ChartedSpace H G] [Group G] [LieGroup I ∞ G]

-- `S.mulInvariantFoliation` is a `Foliation I 1 G`, whose type takes an `IsManifold I (1 + 1) G`
-- instance. Instance search does not identify `1 + 1` with the `2` of the `IsManifold I 2 G`
-- instance coming from `LieGroup I ∞ G`, so it is provided here, as in the file defining
-- `LieSubalgebra.mulInvariantFoliation`.
local instance : IsManifold I (1 + 1) G := inferInstanceAs (IsManifold I 2 G)

variable [I.Boundaryless]

/-- The smooth leaf through the identity of the left-invariant foliation of `S`, with its
intrinsic manifold structure. -/
private abbrev integralLeaf (S : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)) :
    IntegralManifold (I := I) ((⊤ : ℕ∞) : ℕ∞ω) (S.mulInvariantFoliation (I := I)).distribution
      (finrank ℝ S) :=
  (S.mulInvariantFoliation (I := I)).isInvolutiveDistribution.leaf (m := ⊤) (r := ∞) le_top
    (by simp) (S.isContMDiffDistribution_mulInvariantFoliation (by simp)) 1

private instance (S : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)) :
    ConnectedSpace (integralLeaf S).carrier :=
  (S.mulInvariantFoliation (I := I)).isInvolutiveDistribution.connectedSpace_leaf le_top
    (by simp) (S.isContMDiffDistribution_mulInvariantFoliation (by simp)) 1

private theorem injective_integralLeaf (S : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)) :
    Injective (integralLeaf S).map :=
  (S.mulInvariantFoliation (I := I)).isInvolutiveDistribution.map_leaf_injective le_top (by simp)
    (S.isContMDiffDistribution_mulInvariantFoliation (by simp)) 1

/-- The smooth leaf through the identity parametrizes the integral leaf subgroup. -/
private theorem range_integralLeaf (S : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)) :
    range (integralLeaf S).map = (S.integralLeafSubgroup (I := I) : Set G) := by
  rw [coe_integralLeafSubgroup]
  exact (S.mulInvariantFoliation (I := I)).range_leaf_distribution le_top (by simp)
    (S.isContMDiffDistribution_mulInvariantFoliation (by simp)) 1

/-- The smooth leaf through the identity is in bijection with the integral leaf subgroup. -/
private def leafEquiv (S : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)) :
    (integralLeaf S).carrier ≃ S.integralLeafSubgroup (I := I) :=
  (Equiv.ofInjective _ (injective_integralLeaf S)).trans (Equiv.subtypeEquivRight fun g ↦ by
    rw [← SetLike.mem_coe, ← range_integralLeaf])

private instance (S : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)) :
    Group (integralLeaf S).carrier :=
  (leafEquiv S).group

/-- The parametrization of the smooth leaf through the identity, as a homomorphism. -/
private def leafHom (S : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)) :
    (integralLeaf S).carrier →* G :=
  (S.integralLeafSubgroup (I := I)).subtype.comp (leafEquiv S).mulEquiv.toMonoidHom

private theorem coe_leafHom (S : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)) :
    ⇑(leafHom S) = (integralLeaf S).map :=
  rfl

private theorem contMDiff_leafHom (S : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)) :
    ContMDiff (𝓡 (finrank ℝ S)) I ∞ (leafHom S) :=
  (integralLeaf S).isImmersion.contMDiff

/-- The differential at the identity of the smooth leaf through the identity has image the image
of `S` in the tangent space at the identity. -/
private theorem range_mfderiv_leafHom_one (S : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)) :
    LinearMap.range (mfderiv (𝓡 (finrank ℝ S)) I (leafHom S) 1).toLinearMap =
      (S.map (leftInvariantDerivationLieEquivGroupLieAlgebra (I := I) (G := G)
        (ContMDiffMul.isInteriorPoint (n := ∞) (by simp) 1)).toLieHom).toSubmodule := by
  have h := (integralLeaf S).range_mfderiv 1
  rw [← coe_leafHom] at h
  -- `h` describes the image as the fibre of the distribution at `leafHom S 1`, a submodule of the
  -- tangent space there; it is the fibre at `1` once `leafHom S 1 = 1` is substituted.
  have key : ∀ x : G, x = 1 → ∀ V : Submodule ℝ (TangentSpace I x),
      V = (S.mulInvariantFoliation (I := I)).distribution x →
        (V : Submodule ℝ (GroupLieAlgebra I G)) =
          (S.map (leftInvariantDerivationLieEquivGroupLieAlgebra (I := I) (G := G)
            (ContMDiffMul.isInteriorPoint (n := ∞) (by simp) 1)).toLieHom).toSubmodule := by
    rintro x rfl V rfl
    rw [mulInvariantFoliation_distribution]
    exact mulInvariantDistribution_one
  exact key _ (map_one _) _ h

variable [SecondCountableTopology G]

/-- A smooth map into `G` with values in the integral leaf subgroup lifts to a smooth map into
the smooth leaf through the identity. -/
private theorem contMDiff_of_leafHom_comp {F : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup F] [NormedSpace ℝ F]
    {A : Type*} [TopologicalSpace A] {J : ModelWithCorners ℝ F A}
    {P : Type*} [TopologicalSpace P] [ChartedSpace A P]
    (S : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)) {f : P → (integralLeaf S).carrier}
    (hf : ContMDiff J I ∞ (leafHom S ∘ f)) :
    ContMDiff J (𝓡 (finrank ℝ S)) ∞ f := by
  obtain ⟨h, ⟨hh, hcomp⟩, -⟩ :=
    (S.mulInvariantFoliation (I := I)).isInvolutiveDistribution.existsUnique_contMDiff_factor_leaf
      (m := ⊤) (r := ∞) le_top (by simp) (S.isContMDiffDistribution_mulInvariantFoliation (by simp))
      (n := ∞) le_rfl hf
      (by rintro _ ⟨p, rfl⟩; exact mem_range_self _)
  have hfh : f = h := funext fun p ↦ injective_integralLeaf S (congrFun hcomp p).symm
  exact hfh ▸ hh

private instance (S : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)) :
    LieGroup (𝓡 (finrank ℝ S)) ∞ (integralLeaf S).carrier where
  contMDiff_mul := contMDiff_of_leafHom_comp S <| by
    simp only [comp_def, map_mul]
    exact ((contMDiff_leafHom S).comp contMDiff_fst).mul ((contMDiff_leafHom S).comp contMDiff_snd)
  contMDiff_inv := contMDiff_of_leafHom_comp S <| by
    simp only [comp_def, map_inv]
    exact (contMDiff_leafHom S).inv

end Leaf

section Data

attribute [local instance] ImmersedLieSubgroupData.group
  ImmersedLieSubgroupData.topologicalSpace ImmersedLieSubgroupData.normedAddCommGroup
  ImmersedLieSubgroupData.normedSpace ImmersedLieSubgroupData.finiteDimensional
  ImmersedLieSubgroupData.modelTopology ImmersedLieSubgroupData.chartedSpace
  ImmersedLieSubgroupData.lieGroup

variable {E : Type} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E]
  {H : Type} [TopologicalSpace H] {I : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H} [I.Boundaryless]
  {G : Type w} [TopologicalSpace G] [ChartedSpace H G] [Group G] [LieGroup I ∞ G]
  [SecondCountableTopology G]

/-- The integral leaf subgroup of `S` as a connected immersed Lie subgroup, presented by the leaf
through the identity of the left-invariant foliation of `S` with its intrinsic manifold
structure. -/
def integralLeafSubgroupData (S : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)) :
    ImmersedLieSubgroupData I (S.integralLeafSubgroup (I := I)) where
  X := (integralLeaf S).carrier
  E' := EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (finrank ℝ S))
  H' := EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (finrank ℝ S))
  I' := 𝓡 (finrank ℝ S)
  toHom := leafHom S
  injective := injective_integralLeaf S
  range_eq := SetLike.coe_injective (by
    rw [MonoidHom.coe_range, coe_leafHom, range_integralLeaf])
  isImmersion := (integralLeaf S).isImmersion

/-- The differential at the identity of the presentation of the integral leaf subgroup of `S`
has range `S`: the integral leaf subgroup has Lie algebra `S`. -/
@[simp]
theorem range_lieMapToHom_integralLeafSubgroupData
    (S : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)) :
    (S.integralLeafSubgroupData (I := I)).lieMapToHom.range = S := by
  -- Both ranges have the same image under the Lie algebra equivalence `eG`, which is injective.
  have h := LieSubalgebra.toSubmodule_injective <|
    (S.integralLeafSubgroupData (I := I)).range_mfderiv_toHom_one.symm.trans
      (range_mfderiv_leafHom_one S)
  set eG := leftInvariantDerivationLieEquivGroupLieAlgebra
    (ContMDiffMul.isInteriorPoint (I := I) (n := ∞) (by simp) (1 : G))
  ext D
  simpa only [LieSubalgebra.mem_map, LieEquiv.coe_toLieHom, EmbeddingLike.apply_eq_iff_eq,
    exists_eq_right] using SetLike.ext_iff.mp h (eG D)

/-- **Existence of connected immersed Lie subgroups.** Every Lie subalgebra `S` of the Lie algebra
of a second-countable Lie group `G` is the range of the differential of a connected immersed Lie
subgroup of `G`, its integral leaf subgroup. -/
theorem exists_immersedLieSubgroupData_range_lieMapToHom_eq
    (S : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)) :
    ∃ (K : Subgroup G) (d : ImmersedLieSubgroupData I K), d.lieMapToHom.range = S :=
  ⟨_, S.integralLeafSubgroupData, S.range_lieMapToHom_integralLeafSubgroupData⟩

/-- The integral leaf subgroup of a Lie subalgebra is a connected immersed Lie subgroup. -/
theorem isImmersedLieSubgroup_integralLeafSubgroup
    (S : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)) :
    IsImmersedLieSubgroup (I := I) (S.integralLeafSubgroup (I := I)) :=
  S.integralLeafSubgroupData.isImmersedLieSubgroup

/-- A Lie subalgebra lies in the Lie algebra of its integral leaf subgroup. -/
theorem le_lieSubalgebraOfSubgroup_integralLeafSubgroup [T2Space G]
    (S : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)) :
    S ≤ lieSubalgebraOfSubgroup (I := I) (S.integralLeafSubgroup (I := I)) :=
  S.range_lieMapToHom_integralLeafSubgroupData.ge.trans
    S.integralLeafSubgroupData.range_lieMapToHom_le

/-- The integral leaf subgroup of `S` is the subgroup generated by the exponentials of the
elements of `S`. -/
theorem integralLeafSubgroup_eq_closure_lieExp_image [T2Space G]
    (S : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)) :
    S.integralLeafSubgroup (I := I) =
      Subgroup.closure (lieExp '' (S : Set (LeftInvariantDerivation I G))) := by
  simpa only [range_lieMapToHom_integralLeafSubgroupData] using
    (S.integralLeafSubgroupData (I := I)).eq_closure_lieExp_image

/-- The exponential of an element of `S` lies in the integral leaf subgroup of `S`. -/
theorem lieExp_mem_integralLeafSubgroup [T2Space G]
    {S : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)} {X : LeftInvariantDerivation I G}
    (hX : X ∈ S) : lieExp X ∈ S.integralLeafSubgroup (I := I) := by
  rw [integralLeafSubgroup_eq_closure_lieExp_image]
  exact Subgroup.subset_closure ⟨X, hX, rfl⟩

/-- The Lie map of the integral leaf subgroup of `S` has range `S`, as a submodule. -/
theorem range_lieMap_integralLeafSubgroupData
    (S : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)) :
    LinearMap.range (lieMap (S.integralLeafSubgroupData (I := I)).toContMDiffMonoidMorphism
      ).toLinearMap = S.toSubmodule := by
  rw [← LieHom.range_toSubmodule, ImmersedLieSubgroupData.lieMap_toContMDiffMonoidMorphism,
    range_lieMapToHom_integralLeafSubgroupData]

/-- The Lie map of the integral leaf subgroup of `S` takes values in `S`. -/
theorem lieMap_integralLeafSubgroupData_mem
    (S : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G))
    (X : LeftInvariantDerivation (S.integralLeafSubgroupData (I := I)).I'
      (S.integralLeafSubgroupData (I := I)).X) :
    lieMap (S.integralLeafSubgroupData (I := I)).toContMDiffMonoidMorphism X ∈ S := by
  rw [← LieSubalgebra.mem_toSubmodule, ← range_lieMap_integralLeafSubgroupData]
  exact LinearMap.mem_range_self _ X

attribute [local instance] ImmersedLieSubgroupData.connectedSpace in
/-- The integral leaf subgroup of an abelian Lie subalgebra is commutative. -/
theorem commute_integralLeafSubgroupData_of_isLieAbelian
    (S : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)) [IsLieAbelian ↥S]
    (x y : (S.integralLeafSubgroupData (I := I)).X) : Commute x y := by
  have h := ContMDiffMonoidMorphism.commute_of_lie_lieMap_eq_zero
    (S.integralLeafSubgroupData (I := I)).toContMDiffMonoidMorphism
    (S.integralLeafSubgroupData (I := I)).toContMDiffMonoidMorphism
    (fun X Y ↦ by
      simpa using congrArg Subtype.val (trivial_lie_zero S S
        ⟨_, lieMap_integralLeafSubgroupData_mem S X⟩
        ⟨_, lieMap_integralLeafSubgroupData_mem S Y⟩)) x y
  refine (S.integralLeafSubgroupData (I := I)).injective ?_
  simpa [ImmersedLieSubgroupData.toContMDiffMonoidMorphism_apply] using h.eq

attribute [local instance] ImmersedLieSubgroupData.connectedSpace in
/-- The integral leaf subgroups of two Lie ideals with trivial intersection commute with each other
in `G`: the ideals bracket to zero against each other, since `⁅𝔞, 𝔨⁆ ⊆ 𝔞 ⊓ 𝔨 = 0`. -/
theorem _root_.LieIdeal.commute_integralLeafSubgroupData_of_disjoint
    (𝔞 𝔨 : LieIdeal ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)) (h : Disjoint 𝔞 𝔨)
    (x : ((𝔞 : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)).integralLeafSubgroupData
      (I := I)).X)
    (y : ((𝔨 : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)).integralLeafSubgroupData
      (I := I)).X) :
    Commute
      (((𝔞 : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)).integralLeafSubgroupData
        (I := I)).toHom x)
      (((𝔨 : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)).integralLeafSubgroupData
        (I := I)).toHom y) := by
  have hlie : ⁅𝔞, 𝔨⁆ = ⊥ := _root_.eq_bot_iff.mpr ((LieSubmodule.lie_le_inf 𝔞 𝔨).trans h.le_bot)
  have hc := ContMDiffMonoidMorphism.commute_of_lie_lieMap_eq_zero
    ((𝔞 : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)).integralLeafSubgroupData
      (I := I)).toContMDiffMonoidMorphism
    ((𝔨 : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)).integralLeafSubgroupData
      (I := I)).toContMDiffMonoidMorphism
    (fun X Y ↦ (LieSubmodule.lie_eq_bot_iff (I := 𝔞) (N := 𝔨)).mp hlie _
      ((LieIdeal.mem_toLieSubalgebra ℝ _ 𝔞 _).mp (lieMap_integralLeafSubgroupData_mem _ X)) _
      ((LieIdeal.mem_toLieSubalgebra ℝ _ 𝔨 _).mp (lieMap_integralLeafSubgroupData_mem _ Y))) x y
  simpa only [ImmersedLieSubgroupData.toContMDiffMonoidMorphism_apply] using hc

end Data

end LieSubalgebra

namespace TauCeti.Lie.ImmersedLieSubgroupData

variable {E : Type} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E]
  {H : Type} [TopologicalSpace H] {I : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H} [I.Boundaryless]
  {G : Type w} [TopologicalSpace G] [ChartedSpace H G] [Group G] [LieGroup I ∞ G]
  [SecondCountableTopology G]

/-- **Uniqueness of the integral leaf subgroup.** A connected immersed Lie subgroup whose
differential has range `S` is the integral leaf subgroup of `S`. -/
theorem eq_integralLeafSubgroup_of_range_lieMapToHom_eq {K : Subgroup G}
    (d : ImmersedLieSubgroupData I K) {S : LieSubalgebra ℝ (LeftInvariantDerivation I G)}
    (h : d.lieMapToHom.range = S) : K = S.integralLeafSubgroup (I := I) := by
  let _ : T2Space G := I.t2Space_of_lieGroup ∞
  exact d.eq_of_range_lieMapToHom_eq S.integralLeafSubgroupData
    (h.trans S.range_lieMapToHom_integralLeafSubgroupData.symm)

end TauCeti.Lie.ImmersedLieSubgroupData
